;; What `kin/scripts/content-check` allows, per synthetic document, between the HTML's text and the glyph
;; text emon makes of the PDF Chrome printed from it. Exact counts (a ratchet: more, or fewer glyphs
;; than listed, both fail, so an improvement is noticed and recorded). A document not listed allows none.
;;
;;   :extras   glyphs the PDF has and the HTML does not say (counted as a multiset of characters)
;;   :missing  characters the HTML has that no glyph carries
;;
;; THE EXTRAS ARE THE PRINTER'S OWN, every one:
;;   * the running headers, footers and page numbers that the furniture documents draw on every page
;;     (bank-statement, furn-*, invoice) and the repeated table heads (table-multipage-thead), which the
;;     HTML says once;
;;   * the list markers and numbers (footnotes-page's note numbers, lists-*'s `1.` `a.` `IV.`, the ordered
;;     lists of the script documents) and the page numbers of the multipage tables;
;;   * the DRAFT watermark;
;;   * (P2.13, D114) the HYPHENS `hyphens:auto` makes at a line's end: one U+002D glyph per hyphenation point
;;     (the PDF's ToUnicode says `<0010> <0011> <002D>`; poppler writes U+2010 for it). The counts below are
;;     exactly the hyphen points in the documents' `facts.hyphens` (align-justify-hyphen 31, columns-continue
;;     11, columns-newspaper 12), found independently from poppler's lines by tools/synth/build.clj.
;;   An INITIAL that has no glyph (initial-image's W is a PNG, initial-vector's T and L are filled paths) costs
;;     nothing here: the HTML says those letters only in an attribute (`alt`, `data-initial-text`), never in
;;     text, so the page has neither a glyph nor a character of HTML for it. The text-layer initials
;;     (-firstletter, -raised, -firstword, -columns, -rtl, -cjk) have all their glyphs; the floats are painted
;;     before the text (D108 (a)), which is why their `in-order` count is small and is not a claim.
;; THE MISSING ARE THE FONT'S: script-devanagari and script-mixed lose the vowel signs and viramas whose
;; glyphs carry no ToUnicode entry (59 and 8 glyphs are `unknown`, U+FFFD: Skia writes <0000> for the parts
;; of a conjunct), and script-cjk's HTML says 長 (U+9577) where Chrome's ToUnicode says 長's radical variant
;; U+2ED1: the file, not emon, decided that.
{"align-justify-hyphen" {:extras 31}
 "bank-statement" {:extras 354}
 "columns-continue" {:extras 11}
 "columns-newspaper" {:extras 12}
 "footnotes-page" {:extras 2}
 "furn-fixed-dom" {:extras 88}
 "furn-informative" {:extras 180}
 "furn-odd-even" {:extras 57}
 "furn-title-pagenum" {:extras 64}
 "invoice" {:extras 52}
 "lists-basic" {:extras 12}
 "lists-long-multipage" {:extras 174}
 "lists-schemes" {:extras 31}
 "script-cjk" {:extras 7 :missing 1}
 "script-devanagari" {:missing 29}
 "script-hebrew" {:extras 6}
 "script-mixed" {:missing 7}
 "table-multipage-no-thead" {:extras 4}
 "table-multipage-nohead-repeat" {:extras 4}
 "table-multipage-thead" {:extras 76}
 "watermark-draft" {:extras 5}}
